🧠 Most people use AI wrong.

Not because the AI is bad — but because the prompt is weak.

This is Day 2 of my hashtag#ABTalks 60 Days Claude Challenge, and today's topic is one of the most important skills you can learn right now:

👉 Prompt Engineering

Here's the difference:

❌ Weak prompt:
"Write something about productivity."
→ You get a generic, unfocused paragraph that needs 5 rounds of editing.

✅ Engineered prompt:
"Write a 150-word LinkedIn post for working professionals on 3 simple productivity habits. Use a conversational tone, add one emoji per point, and end with a question."
→ You get a publication-ready post. First try.

3 reasons better prompts change everything:

1️⃣ You save time — no more back-and-forth editing loops.
2️⃣ You get relevant outputs — AI understands your goal, audience & format.
3️⃣ You unlock AI's real power — beyond simple questions into real work.

Prompt Engineering isn't a technical skill.
It's a communication skill.

And the better you get at it, the more powerful every AI tool becomes — including Claude.

